@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #f0f0f0
skinparam monochrome true
title Newborn Crying Response Flowchart
start

:Crying;

repeat;
  if (Is the diaper/clothes/bedding dirty?) then (Yes)
    :Change the diaper/clothes/bedding;
  else (No)
    if (Has it been more than 2 hours since the last feeding or milk,\nor signs of hunger such as sticking out tongue, searching for the breast, shaking head?) then (Yes)
      :Feed with breast milk/formula;
    else (No)
      if (Is there straining or groaning, a distended belly?\nIs the baby trying to keep the airway open by tucking their chin?) then (Yes)
        :Try burping the baby;
        if (Is the baby constipated?) then (Yes)
          :Perform abdominal massage or stimulate the anus to encourage a bowel movement;
        else (No)
        endif
      else (No)
      endif
      if (Is the baby sucking on their fingers?) then (Yes)
        :Give a pacifier;
      else (No)
      endif
      :Adjust clothes and diaper to be comfortable;
      :Check if the baby’s nose is blocked, or if hair or threads are tightly wrapped around the body;
      :Gently scratch or massage the head, belly, or feet;
      :Shake a rattle (rattle toy) to move the head or eye gaze;
      :Adjust clothing based on temperature (20–23°C in winter, 26–28°C in summer), and increase humidity;
      :(If not done yet) Swaddle the baby with a cloth;
      if (Is the baby’s temperature above 38.0°C or below 36.0°C, and doesn’t return to normal with changes in clothing?\nIs there continuous vomiting or change in breathing?) then (Yes)
        :Call pediatric emergency consultation\n(dial #8000);
        kill
      else (No)
      endif
      if (Are you holding the baby?) then (No)
        :Try holding the baby;
      else (Yes)
        :Walk for 5 minutes and sit for 5–8 minutes (transport response).\nTap or sway the baby.\nWalk fast, perform squats, or jumping jacks.\nTry "high-high, low-low" games;
        :Change the baby’s holding position (vertical/horizontal), angle;
        :Play white noise, fetal sounds, rain sounds, heartbeat sounds, dryer sounds,\nvacuum cleaner sound, ventilation fan sounds, car engine sounds (VTEC sound, HONDA SOUND SITTER),\nTakamoto Piano CM, Demaekan CM, Poison, Kafka-kun, Noh chanting, poetry singing,\nTomato-chan sound, baseball cheering sounds (jet balloon sounds) via Youtube or a smart speaker;
        :Sing lullabies (e.g., "Kotorin no uta", "Yurikago no uta", Schubert’s lullaby);
        :Crinkle a plastic bag;
        :Blow air on the baby’s face or fan with a hand fan;
        :Hold the baby’s hand;
        :Take a deep breath yourself;
        :Leave the baby for 300 seconds;
      endif
    endif
  endif
repeat while (Did the baby stop crying?) is (No) not (Yes)

stop

@enduml
